id: divine-pulse
name: Divine Pulse
type: standard
actionCost: 1
actionCostMax: 2
kiCostPerBaseTier: 1
kiPerAction: true
attacking: false
requiresTarget: false
usageLimit: 1/round
# A God Maneuver: open where an effect grants it, only in God Ki, 1(bT) Divine Ki Points for each of its 1-2 Actions
# (maneuvers.mjs whyNotGod, spendManeuverCost; use-maneuver.mjs kiPerAction). "This Maneuver functions as the
# Transformation Maneuver and gains its effects" - and there is no Transformation Maneuver yet: until Transformations are
# built, its card says what it does and the table enters the Transformation, the Stress Bonus down and the Force/Magic
# Modifier Bonus up by hand.
godManeuver: true
says: >
  As the Transformation Maneuver. For each Action spent: Stress Bonus 1 lower for it, and that Transformation's Attribute
  Modifier Bonus (FO/MA) 1(T) higher until you leave it.
source: Core Rule
description: >
  A God Maneuver: the Transformation Maneuver, each Action spent on it 1 less Stress Bonus for it and 1(T) more FO/MA
  Modifier Bonus in that Transformation.
text: >
  Divine Pulse [1/Round]: Give your Transformations a spark of godly might.
  –Maneuver Type: Standard
  –Action Cost: Variable (1~2 Actions)
  –DKP Cost: 1(bT) for each Action Spent
  –Effect: This Maneuver functions as the Transformation Maneuver and gains its effects. For each Action spent on this
  Maneuver, reduce your Stress Bonus by 1 for the duration of this Maneuver, but increase the Attribute Modifier Bonus
  (FO/MA) for the Transformation you are attempting to enter by 1(T) until you leave that Transformation.
